00:09:48,547 --> 00:09:51,007
Thank God,
'cause that hair on a baby...

270
00:09:52,426 --> 00:09:55,178
Phoebe, the father
is not here, okay?

271
00:09:55,220 --> 00:09:56,679
I haven't told him yet

272
00:09:56,721 --> 00:09:58,265
and I don't think
I can tell him at all now.

273
00:09:58,306 --> 00:09:59,558
Why not?
Well, I don't know.

274
00:09:59,598 --> 00:10:00,850
Let me think.

275
00:10:00,892 --> 00:10:02,436
I was walking down the street,
thinking

276
00:10:02,477 --> 00:10:05,688
"I'm going to tell the father
today," and then, bam!

277
00:10:05,730 --> 00:10:08,442
Bus?

278
00:10:08,483 --> 00:10:10,193
No, you.

279
00:10:10,235 --> 00:10:11,819
Phoebe, you freaked me out.

280
00:10:11,861 --> 00:10:14,573
You kept saying
how huge this all is.

281
00:10:14,613 --> 00:10:15,782
Well, but it is huge.

282
00:10:15,823 --> 00:10:16,783
I know

283
00:10:16,824 --> 00:10:17,867
but I was just thinking

284
00:10:17,909 --> 00:10:19,286
about how huge it was for me.

285
00:10:19,327 --> 00:10:20,703
I didn't even go

286
00:10:20,745 --> 00:10:22,705
to how huge this is going to be
for the father.

287
00:10:22,747 --> 00:10:24,832
You're thinking about this
way too much.

288
00:10:24,874 --> 00:10:27,168
Just tell him
and get it over with.

289
00:10:27,210 --> 00:10:29,504
It's like ripping off
this Band-Aid.

290
00:10:29,546 --> 00:10:31,965
Quick and painless. Watch.

291
00:10:32,006 --> 00:10:34,008
Ow, mother of...

292
00:10:36,010 --> 00:10:37,345
See?

293
00:10:43,310 --> 00:10:45,019
Ooh. Are we opening presents?

294
00:10:45,061 --> 00:10:46,313
No, no.

295
00:10:46,354 --> 00:10:48,689
I shouldn't
have even opened these.

296
00:10:48,731 --> 00:10:50,609
Joey, I am out of control!

297
00:10:50,650 --> 00:10:53,027
Joey, you have to do me a favor.

298
00:10:53,069 --> 00:10:56,030
No matter what I say,
no matter what I do

299
00:10:56,072 --> 00:10:59,576
please do not let me open
another present, okay?

300
00:10:59,618 --> 00:11:00,952
Okay.

301
00:11:02,412 --> 00:11:03,497
Give me one more.

302
00:11:03,538 --> 00:11:05,081
Okay.

303
00:11:06,291 --> 00:11:07,417
Hey.

304
00:11:07,459 --> 00:11:08,709
Oh, good--

305
00:11:08,751 --> 00:11:09,919
you're here.

306
00:11:09,961 --> 00:11:12,130
Uh, Pheebs, listen, uh

307
00:11:12,172 --> 00:11:13,173
sit down.

308
00:11:13,214 --> 00:11:14,924
I got something
I want to say.

309
00:11:14,966 --> 00:11:16,092
All right.

310
00:11:19,179 --> 00:11:22,599
Um...

311
00:11:22,641 --> 00:11:25,143
it's a scary
world out there--

312
00:11:25,185 --> 00:11:27,562
especially for a single mom.

313
00:11:27,604 --> 00:11:32,984
Now, I've always felt
that you and I have
a special bond, so...

314
00:11:35,362 --> 00:11:38,781
Phoebe Buffay,
will you marry me?

315
00:11:41,993 --> 00:11:44,245
Oh, my God.

316
00:11:45,622 --> 00:11:46,705
Joey...

317
00:11:46,747 --> 00:11:49,376
Oh, yeah, I'll marry you.

318
00:11:50,793 --> 00:11:52,170
You can't marry him.

319
00:11:52,212 --> 00:11:54,381
Hey, lady, your day's over.

320
00:11:54,422 --> 00:11:55,507
It's my turn.

321
00:11:55,549 --> 00:11:56,633
Phoebe...

322
00:11:56,675 --> 00:11:58,134
What? Why can't she marry me?

323
00:11:58,176 --> 00:12:01,762
I can and I will.

324
00:12:01,804 --> 00:12:02,972
She's not pregnant.

325
00:12:03,014 --> 00:12:04,265
It's Rachel.

326
00:12:04,307 --> 00:12:06,267
Rachel's the one who's pregnant,
okay?

327
00:12:06,309 --> 00:12:07,810
Oh, my God.

328
00:12:07,852 --> 00:12:08,978
Hey!

329
00:12:09,020 --> 00:12:10,397
I think he would notice

330
00:12:10,438 --> 00:12:11,898
when you didn't have a baby
in nine months.

331
00:12:11,939 --> 00:12:13,650
It's Joey.

332
00:12:15,235 --> 00:12:17,195
( no audio )

333
00:12:18,697 --> 00:12:19,906
I can't believe it.

334
00:12:19,947 --> 00:12:21,115
Rachel's pregnant?

335
00:12:21,157 --> 00:12:22,325
Mm-hmm.
Yeah.

336
00:12:22,367 --> 00:12:23,577
Well, who's the father?

337
00:12:23,618 --> 00:12:25,286
We don't know.

338
00:12:25,328 --> 00:12:29,290
Oh... I wonder if
it's that dude?

339
00:12:29,332 --> 00:12:31,084
There's a dude?

340
00:12:31,125 --> 00:12:32,835
Who? Who is it?

341
00:12:32,877 --> 00:12:36,130
About a month ago, this guy
spent the night with Rachel.

342
00:12:36,172 --> 00:12:38,508
Now, I didn't see who it was,
but...

343
00:12:43,388 --> 00:12:46,307
Was that story over?

344
00:12:49,603 --> 00:12:51,396
The guy left this.

345
00:12:51,438 --> 00:12:52,439
( gasping )

346
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:54,315
Oh, my God.

347
00:12:54,357 --> 00:12:56,317
I know who the father is.

348
00:13:00,779 --> 00:13:03,491
People have got to
finish their stories.

349
00:13:10,331 --> 00:13:11,499
Uh, excuse me.

350
00:13:11,541 --> 00:13:13,126
Could you take a picture
of us, please?

351
00:13:13,167 --> 00:13:14,168
Oh, of course.

352
00:13:17,589 --> 00:13:19,090
Uh, would you take one
of us?

353
00:13:20,216 --> 00:13:22,385
Uh, yeah. Sure.

354
00:13:23,928 --> 00:13:25,639
Click.

355
00:13:25,680 --> 00:13:27,766
It didn't click.

356
00:13:27,806 --> 00:13:29,309
I heard it.
See?

357
00:13:29,350 --> 00:13:30,602
But there was no flash.

358
00:13:30,644 --> 00:13:32,270
Why won't you
take our picture?

359
00:13:32,312 --> 00:13:35,273
Oh, yeah, I'll-I'll take,
I'll take your picture.

360
00:13:36,691 --> 00:13:39,694
Um, your finger
was covering the lens.

361
00:13:39,736 --> 00:13:40,819
Who are you, Ansel Adams?!

362
00:13:40,861 --> 00:13:41,904
Get out of here!

363
00:13:46,743 --> 00:13:48,119
Look, I feel really bad

364
00:13:48,161 --> 00:13:50,163
about how
I freaked you out before

365
00:13:50,204 --> 00:13:51,623
so, I called the father

366
00:13:51,665 --> 00:13:53,040
and asked him
to meet you here

367
00:13:53,082 --> 00:13:54,334
so you could tell him. Go.

368
00:13:54,375 --> 00:13:55,876
Wha... hey, wait a minute.

369
00:13:55,918 --> 00:13:58,546
Phoebe, how do you even know
who the father is?

370
00:13:58,588 --> 00:14:01,174
I may play the fool at times,
but...

371
00:14:01,215 --> 00:14:04,678
I'm a little more
than just a pretty blonde girl

372
00:14:04,719 --> 00:14:06,805
with an ass that won't quit.

373
00:14:08,306 --> 00:14:09,474
I believe this

374
00:14:09,516 --> 00:14:11,976
belongs to the father
of your baby.

375
00:14:12,018 --> 00:14:14,521
Oh, God.

376
00:14:14,562 --> 00:14:16,105
Oh, he's in
there right now?

377
00:14:16,147 --> 00:14:17,231
Uh-huh.

378
00:14:17,273 --> 00:14:18,733
Now, you can turn around

379
00:14:18,775 --> 00:14:21,736
or you can go in there
and rip the Band-Aid off.

380
00:14:21,778 --> 00:14:23,237
What do you want to do?

381
00:14:23,279 --> 00:14:24,405
Uh...

382
00:14:24,447 --> 00:14:26,032
Let's rip.

383
00:14:26,073 --> 00:14:27,534
Really? Are you sure?

384
00:14:27,575 --> 00:14:28,660
Oh, Phoebe.

385
00:14:28,702 --> 00:14:29,577
Okay, sorry. Yeah.

386
00:14:32,288 --> 00:14:34,040
Hey, Rach.

387
00:14:40,421 --> 00:14:41,756
Why don't you
go up on stage?

388
00:14:41,798 --> 00:14:43,882
I'll get a picture of
you doing the speech.

389
00:14:43,924 --> 00:14:45,426
Okay, okay.

390
00:14:52,975 --> 00:14:55,353
( glasses tinkling )

391
00:15:02,569 --> 00:15:05,363
Will the owner
of a 1995 Buick LeSabre

392
00:15:05,405 --> 00:15:07,323
please see the front desk?

393
00:15:07,365 --> 00:15:09,617
Your car is about to be towed.

394
00:15:12,119 --> 00:15:13,120
That's my car.

395
00:15:14,414 --> 00:15:17,625
A '95 LeSabre?

396
00:15:17,667 --> 00:15:18,668
Yes.

397
00:15:18,710 --> 00:15:20,879
A green LeSabre?

398
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:23,964
Yes.

399
00:15:24,006 --> 00:15:26,760
I'm sorry,
I meant a blue LeSabre.

400
00:15:26,801 --> 00:15:28,219
Yes, green-blue.

401
00:15:31,097 --> 00:15:32,640
Well, go.

402
00:15:32,682 --> 00:15:33,974
Go move it!

403
00:15:35,017 --> 00:15:37,019
Okay. Ready for
the last picture?

404
00:15:37,061 --> 00:15:38,104
Yeah.

405
00:15:38,145 --> 00:15:39,522
Get ready to run.

406
00:15:44,903 --> 00:15:47,196
Congratulations
on your wedding.

407
00:15:54,161 --> 00:15:56,205
So, what's this about?

408
00:15:56,247 --> 00:15:59,667
Rachel has something
that she wants to tell you

409
00:15:59,709 --> 00:16:03,337
and, um, I believe that
this is your red sweater?

410
00:16:03,379 --> 00:16:07,634
No. This is my red sweater.

411
00:16:09,510 --> 00:16:11,345
Oh, no.

412
00:16:13,890 --> 00:16:17,184
Can I get anyone
a coffee, or...

413
00:16:17,226 --> 00:16:19,771
poison? No? Just for me?

414
00:16:19,813 --> 00:16:21,188
Okay.

415
00:16:22,690 --> 00:16:24,567
What's going on,
Rach?

416
00:16:24,609 --> 00:16:27,487
Nothing. Phoebe kind
of made a mistake.

417
00:16:27,528 --> 00:16:30,949
But, you know, you do
wear that sweater a lot.

418
00:16:30,990 --> 00:16:33,827
Are you involved in
some kind of dare?

419
00:16:34,953 --> 00:16:37,664
You know, I'm actually glad
Phoebe called.

420
00:16:43,043 --> 00:16:44,253
I know we broke up

421
00:16:44,295 --> 00:16:45,839
'cause you thought
I wasn't mature enough

422
00:16:45,880 --> 00:16:47,089
but I've really grown up

423
00:16:47,131 --> 00:16:48,549
and I think
we should get back together.

424
00:16:48,591 --> 00:16:52,219
Oh, it's just not
the right time.

425
00:16:52,261 --> 00:16:53,179
It is the right time.

426
00:16:53,220 --> 00:16:54,430
Okay.

427
00:16:54,472 --> 00:16:55,807
I'm ready for more.

428
00:16:55,849 --> 00:16:57,183
Tag...

429
00:16:57,224 --> 00:16:59,727
Come on, Rach,
let's give it another try.

430
00:16:59,769 --> 00:17:02,062
I'm having a baby.

431
00:17:02,104 --> 00:17:04,482
Oh.

432
00:17:10,571 --> 00:17:11,906
You can go.

433
00:17:11,948 --> 00:17:13,407
Thank you.

434
00:17:18,579 --> 00:17:21,123
I don't know how any
of these got opened!

435
00:17:22,834 --> 00:17:24,210
You opened them all?

436
00:17:24,251 --> 00:17:25,461
I know, I know!

437
00:17:25,503 --> 00:17:26,754
I am a terrible person.

438
00:17:26,796 --> 00:17:28,631
Chandler's never going
to trust me

439
00:17:28,673 --> 00:17:30,049
with anything ever again.

440
00:17:30,090 --> 00:17:33,052
Oh, hey,
you got my parents' gift.

441
00:17:33,093 --> 00:17:34,595
Yeah, what is that?

442
00:17:34,637 --> 00:17:37,056
I think it does something
to salami.

443
00:17:39,767 --> 00:17:41,019
Hey

444
00:17:41,060 --> 00:17:42,269
how did it go?

445
00:17:42,311 --> 00:17:43,563
Yeah, what did Tag say?

446
00:17:43,604 --> 00:17:45,356
Tag is not the father.

447
00:17:45,398 --> 00:17:46,941
And Joey knows now?

448
00:17:46,983 --> 00:17:50,570
I do, Rach, I do,
and I am so happy for you.

449
00:17:51,821 --> 00:17:53,948
( chuckles )

450
00:17:53,990 --> 00:17:57,493
Oh, wow, you didn't even try
to unhook my bra.

451
00:17:59,579 --> 00:18:02,415
So, are you ever going
to tell whoever it is?

452
00:18:02,456 --> 00:18:03,750
Yeah, I will.

453
00:18:03,791 --> 00:18:05,209
I'm just not up for it tonight.

454
00:18:05,251 --> 00:18:07,420
Hey, Rach, listen,
no matter what this guy says

455
00:18:07,461 --> 00:18:09,505
I want you to know you're
not going to be alone in this.

456
00:18:09,547 --> 00:18:11,049
I'm not?

457
00:18:11,090 --> 00:18:12,550
No.

458
00:18:12,592 --> 00:18:13,593
Listen, I, uh...

459
00:18:15,762 --> 00:18:19,933
It's a scary world out there,
especially for a single mom.

460
00:18:19,974 --> 00:18:21,059
Aw... Joey...

461
00:18:21,100 --> 00:18:22,476
Uh, I've always felt

462
00:18:22,518 --> 00:18:26,022
like you and I have
this special bond, you know?

463
00:18:26,064 --> 00:18:28,733
So, Rachel Green,
will you marry me?

464
00:18:28,775 --> 00:18:30,443
What?

465
00:18:30,484 --> 00:18:31,694
What?
What?!

466
00:18:31,736 --> 00:18:33,947
Pheebs,
give me the ring back.

467
00:18:33,988 --> 00:18:35,907
No!

468
00:18:35,949 --> 00:18:37,742
Joey, oh, you're so sweet.

469
00:18:37,784 --> 00:18:39,744
You are so, so sweet, honey.

470
00:18:39,786 --> 00:18:42,162
But I'm not looking
for a husband.

471
00:18:46,042 --> 00:18:48,586
I understand.

472
00:18:48,628 --> 00:18:50,713
Now, if you will excuse me

473
00:18:50,755 --> 00:18:53,091
I'm going to go
and lie down.

474
00:18:58,387 --> 00:19:00,640
I can't say that didn't hurt.

475
00:19:02,475 --> 00:19:05,103
But I'll take you back,
Joey Tribbiani.

476
00:19:05,144 --> 00:19:07,313
Uh, yeah, Pheebs,
listen, about that.

477
00:19:07,354 --> 00:19:08,773
Ooh, a Salami Buddy!

478
00:19:08,815 --> 00:19:10,483
There you go.

479
00:19:11,818 --> 00:19:13,778
We're back.

480
00:19:13,820 --> 00:19:15,321
Great! We're hanging
in the kitchen.

481
00:19:15,362 --> 00:19:18,324
Let's stay
in the kitchen.

482
00:19:18,365 --> 00:19:19,951
It's picture time.

483
00:19:19,993 --> 00:19:21,953
Now, you are going
to love these.

484
00:19:21,995 --> 00:19:24,413
Here's a picture of Ross...

485
00:19:24,455 --> 00:19:27,249
and that's me...

486
00:19:27,291 --> 00:19:31,378
and that's me and Ross.

487
00:19:31,420 --> 00:19:34,256
Oh, and here's
a picture of
our first kiss

488
00:19:34,298 --> 00:19:35,633
as a married couple.

489
00:19:35,675 --> 00:19:37,677
Wow, that is
a great picture.

490
00:19:37,718 --> 00:19:38,970
Huh?
Yeah.

491
00:19:39,012 --> 00:19:40,387
And interesting

492
00:19:40,429 --> 00:19:43,390
because I found the cameras
in one of our bags.

493
00:19:46,310 --> 00:19:50,439
Huh. Didn't see that coming.

494
00:19:50,481 --> 00:19:53,484
Okay, so, this
isn't a picture
of our first kiss

495
00:19:53,526 --> 00:19:57,196
but it is a picture
of my first kiss
with, with this lady.

496
00:19:57,237 --> 00:19:58,614
( clearing throat )

497
00:19:58,656 --> 00:19:59,991
Which, by the
look on your face

498
00:20:00,033 --> 00:20:01,200
I'm sure you'll remember

499
00:20:01,241 --> 00:20:02,869
so we don't need...
there's no need...

500
00:20:02,910 --> 00:20:04,120
if we can just...

501
00:20:04,162 --> 00:20:05,830
How about I take
the real pictures

502
00:20:05,872 --> 00:20:07,540
and get them
developed right now?

503
00:20:07,581 --> 00:20:08,958
That would be a good idea.

504
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:10,208
Okay.

505
00:20:13,713 --> 00:20:16,174
You opened all the
presents without me?

506
00:20:16,215 --> 00:20:18,009
I thought we were supposed
to do that together.

507
00:20:18,051 --> 00:20:20,427
You kissed another woman?

508
00:20:21,804 --> 00:20:22,763
Call it even?

509
00:20:22,805 --> 00:20:23,597
Okay.

510
00:20:29,145 --> 00:20:32,481
Well, I'm going to go get these
in some water.

511
00:20:32,523 --> 00:20:34,734
You stole those
from these people's wedding?

512
00:20:34,775 --> 00:20:36,443
No, I took them
from the hotel lobby.

513
00:20:36,485 --> 00:20:38,779
They think they can charge me
for some dirty movie

514
00:20:38,821 --> 00:20:41,574
and a bag of Meshuga Nuts,
they got another thing coming.

515
00:20:45,494 --> 00:20:48,622
Hey, my sweater.

516
00:20:50,541 --> 00:20:53,502
I've been looking for this
for, like, a month.

517
00:20:59,175 --> 00:21:01,094
Oh, my God!
Oh, my God!

518
00:21:08,059 --> 00:21:09,560
Oh, my God!

519
00:21:16,650 --> 00:21:18,069
Hey. How you doing?

520
00:21:18,111 --> 00:21:19,862
Good. Good.
Long time no see.

521
00:21:19,904 --> 00:21:21,030
Yeah.

522
00:21:21,072 --> 00:21:22,073
I like your sweater.

523
00:21:22,115 --> 00:21:24,784
Oh, hey, right
back at you.

524
00:21:24,825 --> 00:21:26,244
( both chuckling )

525
00:21:26,284 --> 00:21:28,662
It's crazy about Rachel, huh?

526
00:21:28,704 --> 00:21:32,833
Yeah. Well, she's
one crazy lady.

527
00:21:32,875 --> 00:21:34,668
So, whose is it?

528
00:21:34,710 --> 00:21:38,756
Um, I, I don't know,
some Italian guy.

529
00:21:38,798 --> 00:21:41,842
Come on, read
your own label.

530
00:21:41,884 --> 00:21:43,677
See you later.
Okay.

531
00:21:43,719 --> 00:21:46,346
( sotto voce ):
He is so weird.

